From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 04:10:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: camss: Serialize buffer completion with stream-off

Prevent the completion interrupt from programming new addresses after
the write masters stop. Wait for in-flight VFE or forwarded CSID
completions before returning the remaining buffers, and clear the
returned slots before the next stream.

This synchronizes the software queue. It does not add a hardware DMA
drain. Verified normal cancellation and stream reopening on both SM8750
camera paths.

Assisted-by: LLM

Wait for the whole SM8750 pipeline to start before handing capture buffers to DMA.
Keep the per-queue startup and completion ordering with the v7
address-update callbacks, including the distinct RAW and PIX updates.

Arm the write masters and CSID port before starting an internal test
pattern generator, which can output a frame immediately. Preserve the
existing startup order for external sensors.

Signed-off-by: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
